ion citation-type="journal">Shen, H.M., A. Peters, B. Baron, X. Zhu, and U. Storb. <year>1998</year>. Mutation of BCL-6 gene in normal B cells by the process of somatic hypermutation of Ig genes. <source>Science.</source> <volume>280</volume>:<fpage>1750</fpage>&#x02013;1752.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9624052</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib29"><label>29</label><citation citation-type="journal">Gordon, M.S., C.M. Kanegai, J.R. Doerr, and R. Wall. <year>2003</year>. Somatic hypermutation of the B cell receptor genes B29 (Igbeta, CD79b) and mb1 (Igalpha, CD79a). <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>100</volume>:<fpage>4126</fpage>&#x02013;4131.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12651942</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib30"><label>30</label><citation citation-type="journal">Muschen, M., D. Re, B. Jungnickel, V. Diehl, K. Rajewsky, and R. Kuppers. <year>2000</year>. Somatic mutation of the CD95 gene in human B cells as a side-effect of the germinal center reaction. <source>J. Exp. Med.</source> <volume>192</volume>:<fpage>1833</fpage>&#x02013;1840.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11120779</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib31"><label>31</label><citation citation-type="journal">Kotani, A., N. Kakazu, T. Tsuruyama, I.M. Okazaki, M. Muramatsu, K. Kinoshita, H. Nagaoka, D. Yabe, and T. Honjo. <year>2007</year>. Activation-induced cytidine deaminase (AID) promotes B cell lymphomagenesis in Emu-cmyc transgenic mice. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>104</volume>:<fpage>1616</fpage>&#x02013;1620.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17251349</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib32"><label>32</label><citation citation-type="journal">Okazaki, I.M., H. Hiai, N. Kakazu, S. Yamada, M. Muramatsu, K. Kinoshita, and T. Honjo. <year>2003</year>. Constitutive expression of AID leads to tumorigenesis. <source>J. Exp. Med.</source> <volume>197</volume>:<fpage>1173</fpage>&#x02013;1181.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12732658</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib33"><label>